## Core Entities

List the main data models. Each entity must have:
- UUID primary key
- `created_at` / `updated_at` timestamps
- Explicit `ondelete` behavior on all foreign keys

### Example: Connection
```
Connection
├── id: UUID (PK)
├── name: str (required)
├── connection_type: enum ["postgresql", "mysql", "mongodb"] (required)
├── role: enum ["source", "target"] (required)
├── host: str (required)
├── port: int (required)
├── database_name: str (required)
├── status: enum ["unchecked", "ok", "error"] (default: "unchecked")
├── created_at: datetime
└── updated_at: datetime
```

### Example: MigrationJob
```
MigrationJob
├── id: UUID (PK)
├── name: str (required)
├── source_connection_id: UUID (FK → Connection, ondelete=SET NULL)
├── target_connection_id: UUID (FK → Connection, ondelete=SET NULL)
├── status: enum ["draft", "ready", "running", "completed", "failed"] (default: "draft")
├── scheduled_at: datetime (optional)
├── created_at: datetime
└── updated_at: datetime
```

